--returns whether node has declarations not inside local blocks
--this does NOT tell whether the procedure raises errors, but,
--whether finding the procedure descriptor may raise errors 
--side effect: changes blockNode (also uses C2CIntCodeUtils.NewVariableId, parent)
--generates new variable, but not yet declared
--constancy required, not error-freeness (evaluation order!)
--DoIt
--don't clobber IntCode tree while debugging other parts
--check to make sure the recursion starts right at this point
--for each lambda call VisitLabels
--and replace id of unused labels
--returns "bits" rightadjusted bits from location "from"
--oCkApply = outer bounds checking apply
--When called, oBckApply oper most be a check operation, lt, unsigned, <= one word
--eliminate masking constants and bound checks
--reduce frequent flags where problems are to be expected
--also compute size of largest dummy
--fix converts of mesa errors from 0 bits to 1 bit
This case does constant folding.  There are some few cases where the mimosa front end might miss the folding of a constant.  I wouldn't consider them worth this effort, but: In these cases a C compiler might get confused whether to use signed or unsigned arithmetic.  I decided that I'd rather introduce constant folding then lots of casts to unsigned...
--don't do that, size may be wrong
IF field.base.bits=var.bits AND field.start=0 THEN {
--field is complete record
RETURN [field.base]; 
};
--return new, modified constant if possible
--we've got it!
--eliminate masking over bound checks if possible
--we've got it!
--try to get rid of multi dimensional packed arrays
--now field can be removed or changed, but
--check if removing field actually helps...
doReplace _ lhs;
--avoids direct visit of addr
--don't recurse on the var itself!
